    "authorAssociation": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.completion\n\n### Question\n\nIs there a way to retrigger file path completion? (`<C-x><C-f>`)\r\n\r\nWhen I'm completing file paths, I usually want to keep autocomplete open until I reach a file. So currently, I have to keep triggering the autocompletion with `<C-x><C-f>` after every completion selection of a folder.\r\n\r\nI think a better workflow would be to automatically retrigger (file path) autocompletion, and require users to manually close.",
    "bodyHTML": "<h3 dir=\"auto\">Contributing guidelines</h3>\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Completed task\" checked=\"\"> I have read <a href=\"https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\">CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Module(s)</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">mini.completion</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Question</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Is there a way to retrigger file path completion? (<code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;C-x&gt;&lt;C-f&gt;</code>)</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">When I'm completing file paths, I usually want to keep autocomplete open until I reach a file. So currently, I have to keep triggering the autocompletion with <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;C-x&gt;&lt;C-f&gt;</code> after every completion selection of a folder.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I think a better workflow would be to automatically retrigger (file path) autocompletion, and require users to manually close.</p>",
    "bodyText": "Contributing guidelines\n\n I have read CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\n\nModule(s)\nmini.completion\nQuestion\nIs there a way to retrigger file path completion? (<C-x><C-f>)\nWhen I'm completing file paths, I usually want to keep autocomplete open until I reach a file. So currently, I have to keep triggering the autocompletion with <C-x><C-f> after every completion selection of a folder.\nI think a better workflow would be to automatically retrigger (file path) autocompletion, and require users to manually close.",
