            "authorAssociation": "NONE",
            "body": "~~Check out [phoenix.nvim](https://github.com/nvimdev/phoenix.nvim), it starts an in-process LSP server (as mini.snippets would do) for buffer & path completions.~~\r\n\r\nOops, I mistakenly read your title as \"register file path completion.\" 😂 Sorry for bothering! But I tried that plugin, and you can always trigger path completion using `force_twostep` (`<C-Space>` by default).",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\"><del>Check out <a href=\"https://github.com/nvimdev/phoenix.nvim\">phoenix.nvim</a>, it starts an in-process LSP server (as mini.snippets would do) for buffer &amp; path completions.</del></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Oops, I mistakenly read your title as \"register file path completion.\" 😂 Sorry for bothering! But I tried that plugin, and you can always trigger path completion using <code class=\"notranslate\">force_twostep</code> (<code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;C-Space&gt;</code> by default).</p>",
