        {
            "author": {
                "avatarUrl": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/24854248?u=d09fd974c6720eba3039db6beb2f1c1efecdb51d&v=4",
                "login": "echasnovski",
                "resourcePath": "/echasnovski",
                "url": "https://github.com/echasnovski"
            },
            "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
            "body": "I don't think in its current form this is a 'mini.completion' question, unless you have `<C-x><C-f>` set up as fallback completion (which would be somewhat of a waste, really).\r\n\r\nBut the general [idea from @loichyan](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/discussions/1995#discussioncomment-14356892) is the best approach though when it comes to 'mini.completion': somehow create an in-process LSP server that would 1) provide path completion and 2) have path separator be a dedicated completion trigger. This way 'mini.completion' will be automatically triggered until user presses path separators.\r\n\r\nIf 'nvimdev/phoenix.nvim' works, then it is probably a good way to achieve that.",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">I don't think in its current form this is a 'mini.completion' question, unless you have <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;C-x&gt;&lt;C-f&gt;</code> set up as fallback completion (which would be somewhat of a waste, really).</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">But the general <a href=\"https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/discussions/1995#discussioncomment-14356892\" data-hovercard-type=\"discussion\" data-hovercard-url=\"/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/discussions/1995/hovercard?comment_id=14356892\">idea from @loichyan</a> is the best approach though when it comes to 'mini.completion': somehow create an in-process LSP server that would 1) provide path completion and 2) have path separator be a dedicated completion trigger. This way 'mini.completion' will be automatically triggered until user presses path separators.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">If 'nvimdev/phoenix.nvim' works, then it is probably a good way to achieve that.</p>",
            "bodyText": "I don't think in its current form this is a 'mini.completion' question, unless you have <C-x><C-f> set up as fallback completion (which would be somewhat of a waste, really).\nBut the general idea from @loichyan is the best approach though when it comes to 'mini.completion': somehow create an in-process LSP server that would 1) provide path completion and 2) have path separator be a dedicated completion trigger. This way 'mini.completion' will be automatically triggered until user presses path separators.\nIf 'nvimdev/phoenix.nvim' works, then it is probably a good way to achieve that.",
