        {
            "author": {
                "avatarUrl": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73006950?u=1ce7ce5123475913f200da68734e106e7c9ecab7&v=4",
                "login": "loichyan",
                "resourcePath": "/loichyan",
                "url": "https://github.com/loichyan"
            },
            "authorAssociation": "NONE",
            "body": "[\\@echasnovski's answer](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/discussions/1995#discussioncomment-14359906) just inspired me that auto retriggering could be done through an autocommand :D\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nvim.api.nvim_create_autocmd(\"InsertCharPre\", {\r\n  callback = function()\r\n    -- It's better to use a more robust logic to check\r\n    -- whether the leaing path-like string is a real path,\r\n    -- for example, check if it exits on the disk.\r\n    if vim.v.char ~= \"/\" then return end\r\n\r\n    -- Avoid duplicate `/`\r\n    local line, cur = vim.api.nvim_get_current_line(), vim.api.nvim_win_get_cursor(0)\r\n    local prev_char = line:sub(cur[2], cur[2])\r\n    if prev_char == \"/\" then vim.v.char = \"\" end\r\n\r\n    -- Force path completion\r\n    local keys = vim.api.nvim_replace_termcodes(\"<C-x><C-f>\", true, true, true)\r\n    vim.api.nvim_feedkeys(keys, \"n\", false)\r\n  end,\r\n})\r\n```",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\"><a href=\"https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/discussions/1995#discussioncomment-14359906\" data-hovercard-type=\"discussion\" data-hovercard-url=\"/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/discussions/1995/hovercard?comment_id=14359906\">@echasnovski's answer</a> just inspired me that auto retriggering could be done through an autocommand :D</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-lua notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"vim.api.nvim_create_autocmd(&quot;InsertCharPre&quot;, {\n  callback = function()\n    -- It's better to use a more robust logic to check\n    -- whether the leaing path-like string is a real path,\n    -- for example, check if it exits on the disk.\n    if vim.v.char ~= &quot;/&quot; then return end\n\n    -- Avoid duplicate `/`\n    local line, cur = vim.api.nvim_get_current_line(), vim.api.nvim_win_get_cursor(0)\n    local prev_char = line:sub(cur[2], cur[2])\n    if prev_char == &quot;/&quot; then vim.v.char = &quot;&quot; end\n\n    -- Force path completion\n    local keys = vim.api.nvim_replace_termcodes(&quot;&lt;C-x&gt;&lt;C-f&gt;&quot;, true, true, true)\n    vim.api.nvim_feedkeys(keys, &quot;n&quot;, false)\n  end,\n})\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">api</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">nvim_create_autocmd</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>InsertCharPre<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>, {\n  <span class=\"pl-en\">callback</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">function</span>()\n    <span class=\"pl-c\"><span class=\"pl-c\">--</span> It's better to use a more robust logic to check</span>\n    <span class=\"pl-c\"><span class=\"pl-c\">--</span> whether the leaing path-like string is a real path,</span>\n    <span class=\"pl-c\"><span class=\"pl-c\">--</span> for example, check if it exits on the disk.</span>\n    <span class=\"pl-k\">if</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">v</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">char</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">~=</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>/<span class=\"pl-pds\">\" </span></span><span class=\"pl-k\">then</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">return</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">end</span>\n\n    <span class=\"pl-c\"><span class=\"pl-c\">--</span> Avoid duplicate `/`</span>\n    <span class=\"pl-k\">local</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">line</span>, <span class=\"pl-smi\">cur</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">api</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">nvim_get_current_line</span>(), <span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">api</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">nvim_win_get_cursor</span>(<span class=\"pl-c1\">0</span>)\n    <span class=\"pl-k\">local</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">prev_char</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-en\">line</span>:<span class=\"pl-c1\">sub</span>(<span class=\"pl-smi\">cur</span>[<span class=\"pl-c1\">2</span>], <span class=\"pl-smi\">cur</span>[<span class=\"pl-c1\">2</span>])\n    <span class=\"pl-k\">if</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">prev_char</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">==</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>/<span class=\"pl-pds\">\" </span></span><span class=\"pl-k\">then</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">v</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">char</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span><span class=\"pl-pds\">\" </span></span><span class=\"pl-k\">end</span>\n\n    <span class=\"pl-c\"><span class=\"pl-c\">--</span> Force path completion</span>\n    <span class=\"pl-k\">local</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">keys</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">api</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">nvim_replace_termcodes</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>&lt;C-x&gt;&lt;C-f&gt;<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-c1\">true</span>, <span class=\"pl-c1\">true</span>, <span class=\"pl-c1\">true</span>)\n    <span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">api</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">nvim_feedkeys</span>(<span class=\"pl-smi\">keys</span>, <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>n<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-c1\">false</span>)\n  <span class=\"pl-k\">end</span>,\n})</pre></div>",
            "bodyText": "@echasnovski's answer just inspired me that auto retriggering could be done through an autocommand :D\nvim.api.nvim_create_autocmd(\"InsertCharPre\", {\n  callback = function()\n    -- It's better to use a more robust logic to check\n    -- whether the leaing path-like string is a real path,\n    -- for example, check if it exits on the disk.\n    if vim.v.char ~= \"/\" then return end\n\n    -- Avoid duplicate `/`\n    local line, cur = vim.api.nvim_get_current_line(), vim.api.nvim_win_get_cursor(0)\n    local prev_char = line:sub(cur[2], cur[2])\n    if prev_char == \"/\" then vim.v.char = \"\" end\n\n    -- Force path completion\n    local keys = vim.api.nvim_replace_termcodes(\"<C-x><C-f>\", true, true, true)\n    vim.api.nvim_feedkeys(keys, \"n\", false)\n  end,\n})",
