                {
                    "author": {
                        "avatarUrl": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/24854248?u=d09fd974c6720eba3039db6beb2f1c1efecdb51d&v=4",
                        "login": "echasnovski",
                        "resourcePath": "/echasnovski",
                        "url": "https://github.com/echasnovski"
                    },
                    "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
                    "body": "Yep, that's another way to achieve this.\r\n\r\nOne thin I like to do is to remove the extra `vim.api.nvim_replace_termcodes` and/or `vim.keycode` calls from the code and use raw values instead (maybe with a small comment). So two `simulate_keypress '<c-x>'` and `simulate_keypress '<c-f>'` can be a single `vim.api.nvim_feedkeys('\\24\\6', 'm', false)`",
                    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">Yep, that's another way to achieve this.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">One thin I like to do is to remove the extra <code class=\"notranslate\">vim.api.nvim_replace_termcodes</code> and/or <code class=\"notranslate\">vim.keycode</code> calls from the code and use raw values instead (maybe with a small comment). So two <code class=\"notranslate\">simulate_keypress '&lt;c-x&gt;'</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">simulate_keypress '&lt;c-f&gt;'</code> can be a single <code class=\"notranslate\">vim.api.nvim_feedkeys('\\24\\6', 'm', false)</code></p>",
